    "role": "hardened",
    "tier": 3,
    "factionId": "",
    "notes": "<p>The metaphysical embodiment of war itself — not a soldier fighting for a cause; the cause. Fifteen feet of rusted swords, broken spears, dented shields and twisted plate, swirling with ghostly green energy, four arms each ending in a different brutal weapon. It forms in the hearts of battlefields where conflict raged for centuries. It will arm one side of a fight solely to turn on them later. Its only goal is that the battle never ends.</p><p><strong>Qliphah:</strong> Thagirion, the Conflicts — the Hull of Tiferet. The balance point of the Tree, replaced by a blade's edge.</p><p><em>Mal's note: 'It cannot be Calmed. It CAN be bored. No one has ever survived long enough to bore it. Aim for the flail arm first.'</em></p>",
